(The Dhargad Watershed is an integral tributary catchment within the Jaigan River basin in District Bageshwar,) Tj
T* (Uttarakhand. Perennial springs \(Dharas\) and traditional subterranean recharge step-wells \(Naulas\) have formed) Tj
T* (the lifeline of drinking water and terraced agriculture for generations in Jatha and Pass villages. Over recent) Tj
T* (decades, intensified monsoonal runoff, structural fracture dislocation, and changes in vegetative land cover have) Tj
T* (severely reduced lean-season spring discharge, precipitating acute seasonal water scarcity.) Tj
